omggif is a JavaScript implementation of a GIF 89a encoder and decoder.

https://github.com/deanm/omggif


Decoding
========

GifReader decodes from a buffer holding the entire file:

    var reader = new omggif.GifReader(buffer);
    var pixels = new Uint8Array(reader.width * reader.height * 4);
    reader.decodeAndBlitFrameRGBA(0, pixels);

GifStreamReader decodes incrementally as bytes arrive (network, disk, ...),
so peak memory stays bounded by the canvas and a single frame rather than
the whole file.  Header parsing, LZW decompression and canvas compositing
all advance frame by frame:

    var reader = new omggif.GifStreamReader();  // or {format: 'bgra'}
    reader.onheader = function(header) { ... };
    reader.onframe = function(frame, framePixels, canvas) {
      // framePixels: this frame blitted onto a transparent canvas-sized
      // buffer, identical to decodeAndBlitFrameRGBA into a zeroed buffer.
      // canvas: the running animation composite with disposal applied.
      // Both buffers are reused between frames -- copy to retain them.
    };
    reader.onend = function() { ... };
    reader.push(chunk);  // Uint8Array/Buffer, as data becomes available
    reader.finish();     // Signal end of input

Run the streaming acceptance test (frame-hash equality against the
whole-file decoder plus a peak-memory comparison on a long GIF):

    node test_streaming.js


